1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,600
(Sheldon:)with no semantic content at all?

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,600
(Penny:)My mirth. Classic.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,140
(Sheldon:)Is there a station
coming up

4
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:11,610
(Sheldon:)where I can board your
giggling train of thought?

5
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:13,780
(Penny:)It's not a big deal, Sheldon.

6
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:15,540
(Penny:)It's just,
ever since Leonard's been

7
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:18,010
(Penny:)dating Raj's sister,
I've had to keep my distance.

8
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:20,920
(Penny:)I don't get to hear
all your jibber-jabber.

9
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,280
Jibber-jabber?!

10
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,920
(Sheldon:)I don't jibber-jabber.

11
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,890
(Penny:)What are you doing
at work these days?

12
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:29,090
(Sheldon:)Oh, I'm working on
time-dependent backgrounds

13
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:30,490
(Sheldon:)in string theory,

14
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:32,020
(Sheldon:)specifically quantum
field theory

15
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:34,330
in "d-dimensional"
de Sitter space.

16
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:38,660
Okay, come on, even you have
to admit that's jibber-jabber.

17
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,100
(Sheldon:)Interesting, do you know

18
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,270
(Sheldon:)where the phrase
"jibber-jabber" comes from?

19
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,740
(Howard:)Oh, my God,
you're about to jibber-jabber

20
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,710
(Penny:)about jibber-jabber.

21
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,010
(Leonard:)Howard and his mother
are at the hospital.

22
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,810
(Leonard:)- Come on, we gotta go.
- Oh, my God! What happened?

23
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:57,010
(Leonard:)I don't know, I just got a text.
Come on, hurry.

24
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:01,020
(Howard(reading a text):)Okay.

